{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774736,"nonce":"q5uUbmveq9N0cNJMwyTaL7+NtyU=","title":"feat(secrets): the coverage matrix becomes the scope editor (ADR-0060 slice 2)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #75 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/adr-0060-secret-matrix-editor` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-25T16:59:19Z · Merged: 2026-07-25T17:58:03Z\n\nSecond slice of ADR-0060. Closes git-bug `af1ffae`.\n\n**Stacked on #74** — review that first; retarget this to `main` once it lands.\n\nAn **environment-scoped secret had no UI at all.** The repo Secrets tab wrote\nonly at repo scope, the Environments tab is rules-only, and the ADR-0037\ncoverage matrix was read-only — so it could show you a gap it gave you no\nway to fill. Setting a per-environment value meant raw HTTP.\n\nThe matrix *is* the editor. Rows are keys; columns are scopes —\n**Repository default** first, then one per Environment — and clicking a cell\nwrites or clears a value **at that scope**, through the existing scoped\n`/v1/secrets` endpoints. One grid rather than per-environment editors,\nbecause secrets are one key-addressed namespace resolved by scope\n(ADR-0037 §C): *\"does prod override the default?\"* is a question you answer\nby reading along a row.\n\nTwo things the read model was missing:\n\n1. **A repo-default column** — the scope everything falls through to is now\n   visible and writable, not implied.\n2. **`inherited_from`** (`repo` | `org`) per inherited cell. Collapsing both\n   broader scopes into one \"inherited\" made an edit unexplainable; now the\n   editor says *\"overrides the org value here only\"* and names what clearing\n   would fall back to.\n\nA `secret_unset_markers` table behind a new `SecretCoverageStore` port.\nDeliberately **separate from `EnvironmentStore`**: it is advisory — never read\non a run path, never blocks a deploy — so a deployment that can't store\nmarkers still gets a working matrix.\n\nThe invariant worth stating: **a marker can only silence a genuinely empty\ncell.** Give that cell a value and the value shows, because a silenced cell\nthat actually resolves would lie about coverage. Asserted both ways.\n\nCell vocabulary: `●` set here · `○` inherited (hover for which scope) · `–`\nunset · `⊘` intentionally unset.\n\n`crates/scarab-server/tests/secret_matrix_editor.rs` — 4 tests against **real\nPostgres**, checking `resolve` and not merely the read model that produced it\n(the model could be right while the write went to the wrong scope):\n\n- env override wins; unset envs fall through to the repo default; clearing one\n  scope hands it back without touching the other\n- cells name the scope they'd override (`org` vs `repo`)\n- silencing annotates an empty cell, never masks a value, survives a\n  set-then-clear round trip, and is idempotent both directions\n- the repo-default column is silenceable too\n\nPlus: existing `environments.rs` matrix assertions updated to the new shape ·\nfull server suite **196 passed** with `SCARAB_TEST_REQUIRE_PG=1` · `npm test`\n72 passed · typecheck, UI build and docs build clean · driven in mock mode\n(inherited cell → *\"Currently inherited from the org. Saving overrides it here\nonly\"*; silenced cell → marker pre-checked).\n\nDocs: the Secrets page section rewritten from \"coverage view\" to \"where you\nset them\", with the cell vocabulary and the reason environments stay\nrules-only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}